{"tool_name":"deepbgc","contents":["biocontainers","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"deepbgc","identifiers":["doi:10.1093/nar/gkz654"],"license":"MIT","summary":"Deepbgc - biosynthetic gene cluster detection and classification","home_url":"https://github.com/Merck/DeepBGC","keywords":["Biosynthetic Pathways","Computational Biology","Data Mining","Deep Learning","Genome","Genome, Bacterial","Multigene Family"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":1},"biotools":{"id":"DeepBGC","home":"https://github.com/Merck/deepbgc","license":"MIT","summary":"A deep learning genome-mining strategy for biosynthetic gene cluster prediction | BGC Detection and Classification Using Deep Learning | DeepBGC: Biosynthetic Gene Cluster detection and classification | DeepBGC detects BGCs in bacterial and fungal genomes using deep learning. DeepBGC employs a Bidirectional Long Short-Term Memory Recurrent Neural Network and a word2vec-like vector embedding of Pfam protein domains. Product class and activity of detected BGCs is predicted using a Random Forest classifier","addition_date":"2019-11-14T18:29:25Z","last_update_date":"2020-12-17T15:22:33Z","tool_type":["Workflow"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:DeepBGC","credit":[{"email":"christopher.woelk@merck.com","name":"Christopher H Woelk","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"danny.bitton@merck.com","name":"Danny A Bitton","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"public"},"function":[{"cmd":"deepbgc pipeline myInputSequence.fa","input":[{"data":{"term":"DNA sequence","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_3494"},"format":[{"term":"FASTA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1929"},{"term":"GenBank format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1936"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"Natural product identification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3803"},{"term":"Text mining","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0306"}]}],"name":"DeepBGC","owner":"Pub2Tools","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/NAR/GKZ654","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 The Author(s) 2019. Published by Oxford University Press on behalf of Nucleic Acids Research.Natural products represent a rich reservoir of small molecule drug candidates utilized as antimicrobial drugs, anticancer therapies, and immunomodulatory agents. These molecules are microbial secondary metabolites synthesized by co-localized genes termed Biosynthetic Gene Clusters (BGCs). The increase in full microbial genomes and similar resources has led to development of BGC prediction algorithms, although their precision and ability to identify novel BGC classes could be improved. Here we present a deep learning strategy (DeepBGC) that offers reduced false positive rates in BGC identification and an improved ability to extrapolate and identify novel BGC classes compared to existing machine-learning tools. We supplemented this with random forest classifiers that accurately predicted BGC product classes and potential chemical activity. Application of DeepBGC to bacterial genomes uncovered previously undetectable putative BGCs that may code for natural products with novel biologic activities. The improved accuracy and classification ability of DeepBGC represents a major addition to in-silico BGC identification.","authors":[{"name":"Bitton D.A."},{"name":"Chang D."},{"name":"Durcak J."},{"name":"Hannigan G.D."},{"name":"Hazuda D.J."},{"name":"Klempir O."},{"name":"Kotowski J."},{"name":"Palicka A."},{"name":"Piizzi G."},{"name":"Prihoda D."},{"name":"Rampula L."},{"name":"Soukup J."},{"name":"Temesi G."},{"name":"Wang R."},{"name":"Woelk C.H."},{"name":"Wurst M."}],"citationCount":25,"date":"2019-10-10T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nucleic acids research","title":"A deep learning genome-mining strategy for biosynthetic gene cluster prediction"},"pmcid":"PMC6765103","pmid":"31400112"}],"topic":[{"term":"Machine learning","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3474"},{"term":"Metabolomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3172"},{"term":"Small molecules","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0154"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"DeepBGC","home":"https://bio.tools/DeepBGC","license":"MIT","summary":"A deep learning genome-mining strategy for biosynthetic gene cluster prediction | BGC Detection and Classification Using Deep Learning | DeepBGC: Biosynthetic Gene Cluster detection and classification | DeepBGC detects BGCs in bacterial and fungal genomes using deep learning. DeepBGC employs a Bidirectional Long Short-Term Memory Recurrent Neural Network and a word2vec-like vector embedding of Pfam protein domains. Product class and activity of detected BGCs is predicted using a Random Forest classifier","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:deepbgc/workflow/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":true,"registration":false},"packages":true,"source_packages":true,"sourcecode":{"free":true,"interpreted":true,"license":true,"public":true,"readme":true,"repository":{"anonymous":true,"online":true}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":187,"citations":[{"count":8,"year":"2020"},{"count":19,"year":"2021"},{"count":19,"year":"2022"},{"count":27,"year":"2024"},{"count":29,"year":"2023"},{"count":40,"year":"2026"},{"count":45,"year":"2025"}],"doi":"10.1093/nar/gkz654","pmcid":"PMC6765103","pmid":"31400112","ref_count":38,"refs":[{"count":1,"year":"-1"},{"count":1,"year":"1977"},{"count":1,"year":"1989"},{"count":1,"year":"1990"},{"count":1,"year":"1997"},{"count":1,"year":"2000"},{"count":1,"year":"2003"},{"count":1,"year":"2007"},{"count":1,"year":"2010"},{"count":2,"year":"1998"},{"count":2,"year":"2004"},{"count":2,"year":"2009"},{"count":2,"year":"2011"},{"count":2,"year":"2012"},{"count":2,"year":"2013"},{"count":2,"year":"2014"},{"coun